].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and third column:\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}z & -3 & ∗ \\\\ -5 & z-8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 6z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${r}_{33}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}z & -3 \\\\ 5 & z-8\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}z & -3 \\\\ 5 & z-8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =z\\cdot (z-8)-(-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-8z+15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${r}_{33}$ is $3$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-8z+15 & =3 \\\\ {z}^{2}-8z+12 & =0 \\\\ (z-2)(z-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=2$ and $z=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-128116/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa65a73-e750-5052-9249-7c096297ae51"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128116"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
